format="epo"><addressbook><name>INAMORI SYOUHEI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIDO OSAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MORISHITA KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UETSUJI TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIMOTO, MASATSUGU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INAMORI, SYOUHEI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIDO, OSAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORISHITA, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UETSUJI, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A thermoelectric module (7) having a heat absorbing surface and a heat radiating surface designed so that the heat radiating surface is heated and the heat absorbing surface is cooled by having an electric current passed therethrough is built in a manifold main body (17), while fluid-receiving cavities (10c, 10d, 20d) are formed between it and at least either the heat absorbing surface or the heat radiating surface, and hollows (10a, 10b, 20a, 20b) extending from outside to the cavities (10c, 10d, 20d) are formed.  Further, installed in the manifold main body (17) are a stirring member for stirring the fluid in the cavities that has a stirring portion (15) integrated with a rotor (16), and a stator (8) fitted on the manifold main body (17), the rotor (16) and stator (8) constituting a motor. In this arrangement, an electric current is passed through the stator (8) to rotate the stirring member (5) in the cavities, causing the fluid to pass through the rotor (16) to reach the cavities (10c, 10d).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un module thermoélectrique (7) présentant une surface thermoabsorbante et une surface thermorayonnante, la surface thermorayonnante étant chauffée et la surface thermoabsorbante refroidie. Ce module thermoélectrique, qui est traversé par un courant, est intégré dans le corps principal d'un collecteur (17). Des cavités réceptrices de liquide (10c, 10d, 20d) sont situées entre le module et au moins soit la surface thermoabsorbante, soit la surface rthermorayonnnante, avec des creux (10a, 10b, 20a, 20b) partant des cavités (10c, 10d, 20d). Par ailleurs, le corps principal de collecteur (17) comporte un élément agitateur qui brasse le liquide contenu dans les cavités. Cet élément agitateur comprend une partie de brassage (15) intégrée à un rotor (16), et un stator (8) monté sur le corps principal de collecteur (17). Le rotor (16) et le stator (8) forment un moteur. Dans ce montage, un courant électrique qui traverse le stator (8) fait tourner l'élément agitateur (5)qui brasse le liquide dans les cavités (10c, 10d) via le rotor (16).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>